# What boot starts once the drivers are running: from the system volume,
# when / is one, or from the initramfs. A shell on the serial line, the
# first, which boot waits for, so that its exit stops the system; its
# terminal is console, which uart serves. wm, the compositor, owns the
# screen through display and keeps windows on it for its clients; vt is
# a terminal in one of them, named vt1, starting its own shell, sh vt1,
# and closing when it exits; and procmon, the System Monitor, is the
# other, the kernel's processes and the memory they are given.
# tests/vt.sh boots tests/vt/etc/system in place of this, with two vts.
start /bin/sh
start /sbin/wm
start /Applications/Terminal.app/vt
start /Applications/Monitor.app/procmon
